# What the Vercel CLI must not upload. It doesn't read .gitignore, and the
# first attempt shipped 485 MB of local build caches before failing on a
# 100 MB file. The build happens on Vercel, so only the source goes up.
# Anchored with a leading slash where a bare name would also match a
# folder deeper in the tree (lib/content is source and has to go up).
/.next
/.next-*
/.git
/node_modules
/test-results
/playwright-report
/coverage
/docs
/design
/content
/tests
/export
/emulator-data
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
serviceAccountKey.json
*-service-account*.json
.env*
!.env.example
# The lesson videos are a 1.1 GB symlink to a folder outside the repo.
# Vercel isn't the place for them (100 MB per-file limit, bandwidth cost),
# so the deployed site serves them from Firebase Storage instead.
/public/videos
